{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "recipe": "Clone baseline, apply setup then previous operations, clone that result, then apply candidate operations. Operations set, remove, or deep-copy an object member at a JSON Pointer; schema selects an entry from schemas. Parse both descriptors with the existing strict V1 parser. inverse swaps the parsed descriptors. Changes are exact [Path, Code] pairs, sorted ordinally by Path then Code.",
  "proofPolicy": {
    "request": "previous subset candidate",
    "responseEventAndErrorDetails": "candidate subset previous",
    "canonicalEquality": "Unchanged, including canonical property-order equivalence",
    "abiEquality": "Patch, including version-only, annotations, and normalized set order",
    "namedReferences": "Names must match. Equality includes all reachable definitions, not just local ref text. Inline/ref and renamed-alias transformations are unclassified Major.",
    "records": "Closed records only; target required names must be guaranteed by source, every source property must be accepted by target, and values/cardinality must be contained. Presence and nullability are independent. Required/property counts supply implicit source cardinality bounds.",
    "stringsArraysMaps": "Contain ordinary string lengths, array/map cardinalities, items, map values and ordinary string keys. Missing minima mean zero; missing maxima mean unbounded. Empty-container shortcuts do not waive generated value/key API checks.",
    "literals": "Ordinary string/boolean/null enums use literal set inclusion without remapping; const must stay equal. Adding/removing enum or const form is unclassified Major. Numeric literals/bounds remain equality-only.",
    "unproved": "Numeric bounds, exact formats, dynamic/any/object-form transformations and changed tagged unions are Major unless the whole named schema graph is exactly ABI-equal. This deliberately does not infer union discriminator remappings or numeric/format implications.",
    "recursion": "Exact named recursive graphs are accepted; any unequal compared graph reaching a cycle is unclassified Major. No coinductive subset guess.",
    "generatedApi": "Removed definitions/errors are Major. Existing definitions not covered by a directional proof must remain graph-equal, including unused definitions. New definitions/error declarations are Minor, but a newly declared error on an existing method is Major.",
    "limits": "65536 proof steps, 128 traversal depth, 1024 UTF-16 code units per JSON Pointer, 64 reasons including the changes-truncated marker. Limit exhaustion is Major analysis-limit-exceeded. Diagnostics never contain schema literals or descriptor bodies."
  },
